When a captured event is waited on by a stream, it places the stream in capture mode if it is not already, and the next item in the stream will have additional dependencies on the nodes in the captured event.
The two streams are then being captured to the same capture graph.
When cross-stream dependencies are present in stream capture, cudaStreamEndCapture() must still be called in the same stream where cudaStreamBeginCapture() was called;

This offers protection without compromising performance.
